{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass\/Step-swift.struct"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass\/step-swift.struct\/color"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass\/Step-swift.struct\/color","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"color","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLBassV4StepV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBass/Step-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bass-step type represents the pitch step of the bass of the current chord within the harmony element. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text attribute indicates how the bass should appear in a score if not using the element contents."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"MXLBass.Step","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass\/Step-swift.struct","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass\/step-swift.struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Step","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Step","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBass":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLBass","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLBass","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bass type is used to indicate a bass note in popular music chord symbols, e.g. G\/C. It is generally not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in functional harmony, as inversion is generally not used in pop chord symbols. As with root, it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"divided into step and alter elements, similar to pitches. The arrangement attribute specifies where the bass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is displayed relative to what precedes it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass","title":"MXLBass","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBass/Step-swift.struct/color":{"title":"color","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass\/step-swift.struct\/color","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass\/Step-swift.struct\/color","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"}}}